// Title: DLL Execution via Rasautou.exe
// Sigma ID: cd3d1298-eb3b-476c-ac67-12847de55813
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Julia Fomina, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects using Rasautou.exe for loading arbitrary .DLL specified in -d option and executes the
//   export specified in -p.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Rasautou/
//   - https://github.com/fireeye/DueDLLigence
//   - https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/10/staying-hidden-on-the-endpoint-evading-detection-with-shellcode.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_rasautou_dll_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rasautou.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "rasdlui.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -d " and ProcessCommandLine contains " -p ")
